# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots httpd 2.4.49 with the vulnerable (traversal-enabled)
# config in the BACKGROUND and then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * httpd is ALREADY RUNNING when the agent starts, which makes the
#     "fixed the config but never restarted the service" case detectable;
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting httpd cannot kill the container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the fix must RESTART httpd, not merely start it.
